st  one  and we do not know at the moment being  how successful books vaccines will be  in other words how much immunization  they  they're  able to provide whether it's 50 or 70  percent or up to 90 percent  and therefore we have to keep in mind  that it is a stepwise approach to  immunity  that we will experience with the  vaccines and this was a broad topic  tonight too  thank you passing the floor now to um  andrei matishak from pravda  you have the flow yeah thank you  and good evening um andrey matshek  slovakia david  my question would be for president  mitchell and  i would like to ask you uh slovak prime  minister mr matovich  said that  that he will brief readers  about slovak experiment using nationwide  antigen testing so could you please uh  describe this intervention  maybe that is if there was any  discussion about it  and if any country said that they would  like to follow slovakia  example thank you in  indeed the the prime minister explained  what's the strategy in his country  regarding the the rapid test  and indeed in many countries there is  an interest for the rapid test because  we have the impression  that with the pcr test those  new rapid tests and that's why we are in  further of a mutual recognition  can help in order to develop a global  strategy  ursula van der leyen just explained how  important it was and it is and it will  be  to develop a strong strategy regarding  the vaccines  but we know that the vaccines will not  solve everything  immediately we will need in parallel to  be more efficient  with the testing with the tracing and  uh the prime minister explained that he  will share with all the colleagues with  all the members  the outcome the results of his  strategy and his project  to organize on a very broad basis  testing in order to be able to isolate  and in order to share with us  after that the data in order to to share  different experiences and to to try to  make  more progress everywhere in europe  thank you we'll take a last question  from naomi o'leary  naomi from the irish times  hi thank you very much for taking my  question um so  just for the commission and president of  underlying you said that you don't  encourage travel now  um and that it's very important that  testing and tracing should be in place  for when things get better in hindsight  was it a mistake to encourage the  resumption of tourism in your  reopen eu plan um  given that we can now see through for  example  genetic examination of the strains of  kovic 19  that travel between states fueled the  resurgence that we're seeing now was  that a short-term economic  um policy in the uh now the in hindsight  thanks  so i have not understood all the parts  of the question but  i have understood that it's about  the uh travel and the question whether  it is appropriate or not unnecessary  travel of course is inappropriate  in the situation we're in at the moment  being  it should be reduced to really necessary  essential travel  and you asked for uh  how do we well how would we judge on the  situation looking back  so what we've seen and what we've  learned is  that after the decrees of the first wave  during summer we obviously  have relaxed some measures  too rapidly and  it is not only a question of travel for  sure not  because you've seen in the whole  discussion we had over the last weeks  but also  tonight that there are many variables  that are crucial for keeping  the virus down and what we have to  keep in mind is that we will have to  fight the virus and we will have to keep  the spread of the virus  low till we have enough immunity through  vaccination  in the population so we'll have to be  very careful with  lifting measures and keep in mind the  most  powerful instrument we have in our mind  in our hands  is how we behave ourselves this is masks  this is social distancing and this is  do not stay in closed rooms with poor  ventilation those three things  are of utmost importance to help to keep  the virus down  thank you madam president this concludes  our press conference for tonight and  see you soon thanks for joining  indeed the mask  [Music]  you
 

